      "meta": [
        { "text": "updated 10 mins ago" },
        { "text": "Sprint 14", "icon": "flag", "tone": "primary" }
      ],
      "steps_done": 1,
      "steps_total": 3,
      "progress_tone": "primary",
      "estimate": "30m",
      "estimate_title": "Estimated 30 minutes",
      "comments": 5,
      "files": 3,
      "assignee": { "name": "Nayan", "handle": "@nayan", "initial": "N", "tone": "primary" },
      "milestone": "%v2.4 Release",
      "due": "Sep 24, 2026",
      "selected": true,
      "detail": {
        "markdown": "### Problem Background & Summary\nUsers report being unable to authenticate or retain session when access tokens expire. Signature verification fails repeatedly on the `/auth/refresh` endpoint during rotation grace period, resulting in a sudden `401 Unauthorized - Invalid Token Signature` redirect.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n1. Log in via standard OAuth2 password credentials grant.\n2. Fast-forward the local JWT expiry window past 15 minutes:\n\n```bash\nexport JWT_ACCESS_TTL=1m\nmake run-auth\n```\n\n3. Trigger any authenticated request from the dashboard.\n4. Observe the refresh call returning `401` instead of a rotated token.\n\n### Expected Behaviour\nThe refresh endpoint should accept tokens signed with the previous key for the length of the rotation grace window and issue a fresh access token signed with the active key.\n\n### Actual Behaviour\nThe validator only loads the active signing key, so every token signed before rotation is rejected as `invalid signature` and the user is logged out mid-session.\n\n### Root Cause\n- Key rotation job replaced `JWT_SECRET` without keeping the previous key in the keyring.\n- `ValidateToken` never consults the `kid` header, so it cannot pick the matching key.\n\n### Proposed Fix\n- [x] Analyze application logs and verify expired JWT secret\n- [ ] Keep the previous key in the keyring for the grace window\n- [ ] Select verification key by `kid`\n- [ ] Return a clear user-facing error when refresh truly fails\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n| Scenario | Expected |\n| --- | --- |\n| Token signed by active key | 200, new token |\n| Token signed by previous key within grace | 200, new token |\n| Token signed by unknown key | 401 with clear message |\n\n### Notes\nSentry issue `AUTH-2291` shows 1,284 events in the last 24h, all from the refresh path.",
        "steps": [
          { "id": "i104-1", "label": "Analyze application logs and verify expired JWT secret", "checked": true, "note": "Verified in Sentry", "note_icon": "done" },
          { "id": "i104-2", "label": "Update JWT validation logic and middleware error handler", "checked": false, "note": "In progress by @nayan", "note_icon": "progress" },
          { "id": "i104-3", "label": "Verify error messages displayed cleanly on client login modal", "checked": false, "note": "Blocked by middleware update", "note_icon": "pending" }
        ],
        "branch": "104-fix-jwt-token-expired",
        "merge_request": "!48 Fix token validation",
        "discussion": [
          { "id": "d1", "author": "Sarah T.", "initial": "S", "tone": "secondary", "time": "18 mins ago", "body": "Checked the auth service logs; secret key rotation caused the mismatch. PR is ready for review." },
          { "id": "d2", "author": "Nayan", "initial": "N", "tone": "primary", "time": "42 mins ago", "body": "Adding the previous key to the keyring should cover the grace window. Will pair with kid-based lookup." },
          { "id": "d3", "author": "Alex M.", "initial": "A", "tone": "neutral", "time": "1 hour ago", "body": "Reproduced locally with JWT_ACCESS_TTL=1m — refresh fails on the first rotation." },
          { "id": "d4", "author": "Elena R.", "initial": "E", "tone": "tertiary", "time": "2 hours ago", "body": "Support is seeing a spike of logout complaints from the EU region." },
          { "id": "d5", "author": "Nayan", "initial": "N", "tone": "primary", "time": "2 hours ago", "body": "Opened this issue from the Sentry alert AUTH-2291." }
        ],
        "activity": [
          { "id": "a1", "time": "10 mins ago", "text": "@nayan checked \"Analyze application logs and verify expired JWT secret\"" },
          { "id": "a2", "time": "45 mins ago", "text": "@sarah linked merge request !48" },
          { "id": "a3", "time": "1 hour ago", "text": "@nayan moved this issue to Do it Now" },
          { "id": "a4", "time": "2 hours ago", "text": "@nayan opened this issue" }
        ]
      }
